# Production environment for /srv/th-labs/.env on the server.
# Copy this file there and fill it in. It is the only place the database
# password and JWT secrets exist — it is never committed and never baked into
# the image.
#
#   chmod 600 /srv/th-labs/.env

# ── PostgreSQL ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
POSTGRES_USER=thlabs
POSTGRES_DB=thlabs
# Required.
POSTGRES_PASSWORD=

# ── JWT ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Both required — compose refuses to start without them.
#   openssl rand -hex 32
JWT_SECRET=
JWT_REFRESH_SECRET=

JWT_EXPIRES_IN=15m
JWT_REFRESH_EXPIRES_IN=7d

# ── Origins ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Comma-separated list of browser origins allowed to call this API. The Studio
# runs on Modal — a different origin — and redeems its handoff code and
# refreshes from the BROWSER, so its origin MUST be here or sign-in there fails
# with an opaque CORS error. Leave unset to use the defaults in api/src/main.ts.
CORS_ORIGINS=https://th-labs.uz,https://www.th-labs.uz,https://aytingchi.uz,https://www.aytingchi.uz,https://isoqovjorabek2--th-labs-dubbing-web.modal.run
APP_URL=https://th-labs.uz

# ── Lemon Squeezy ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Payments are Lemon Squeezy share links plus reads of the LS API. No webhook.
#
# How a purchase becomes credits:
#   1. The Buy button opens the plan's share link with the account's email
#      prefilled (that email is how the order is found again).
#   2. The customer pays on lemonsqueezy.com.
#   3. The API asks LS for the paid orders filed under that email and credits
#      each new one, matched on the order's VARIANT id — once, keyed on the
#      order id. It asks when the buyer returns to /plans/success, and every
#      5 minutes for a day after a checkout was opened, so closing the tab
#      loses nothing. Subscription renewals are polled hourly the same way.
#
# The links and variant ids live in the catalog (admin panel; the seed fills
# the starting ones). Nothing to set here for them.
#
# Set each LS product's redirect / confirmation button link to
# ${APP_URL}/plans/success so buyers come straight back. Optional — the cron
# credits them anyway.
#
# LEMONSQUEEZY_API_KEY is the critical one: without it no purchase can be
# verified, so Buy buttons 503 rather than taking money that cannot be
# credited. Keys are per-mode — a TEST-mode key sees only test orders — so it
# must match the mode of the links in the catalog (currently TEST mode).
# LEMONSQUEEZY_STORE_ID is only needed if the key can see more than one store.
LEMONSQUEEZY_API_KEY=
LEMONSQUEEZY_STORE_ID=

# No FREE_DUB_MAX_SECONDS any more. Every new account is granted credits worth
# one minute of Balanced dubbing (SIGNUP_BONUS_CREDITS in
# api/src/payment/quality-cost.ts), and from then on the balance alone decides
# how much of a video can be dubbed — a short balance dubs the front of it.
# Change the grant or the per-minute tariff in that file, not here.

# ── Deployment ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Only used for the banner the app prints on boot.
PUBLIC_HOST=aytingchi.uz

# Pin to a specific build to roll back; leave unset to track latest.
#   API_IMAGE=ghcr.io/asilbekali/th-labs-full/api:sha-<commit>
# API_IMAGE=
